---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Aff from '../components/Aff.astro';
const title = 'Screening Atlas';
const description = 'Tenant screening rules and report coverage, state by state: application fee caps, what each screening report includes, and where criminal or eviction records may not appear. Every claim is linked to its source.';
const schema = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebSite","name":"Screening Atlas","description":description};
---
<Base title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <h1>Tenant screening, state by state, with sources</h1>
  <p class="lede">Small landlords keep asking the same questions: what can I charge an applicant, what will this report actually show, and why did it come back blank? The answers depend on the state, and sometimes on the county. Screening Atlas answers them one state and one provider at a time, and links every claim to the law or the provider's own page.</p>

  <div class="note"><strong>New: <a href="/tenant-screening-checker-by-state/">Tenant screening checker by state</a>.</strong> Pick your state to see the application fee rule, whether a reusable report waives the fee, where SmartMove can return criminal and eviction records, and which screening packages fit under the cap.</div>

  <div class="note"><strong>New: <a href="/kit/">Landlord Tenant Screening Kit</a>.</strong> A 16-page kit with written screening criteria, application and adverse-action templates, and a state cheat sheet. $29, with a 14-day money-back guarantee.</div>

  <div class="cards">
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/kit/">Landlord Tenant Screening Kit</a></h3><p>Written criteria, application and adverse-action templates, plus a state cheat sheet. $29, with a 14-day money-back guarantee.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/application-fee-caps-by-state/">Application fee caps by state</a></h3><p>Dollar caps, actual-cost rules and outright bans, quoted from each statute. 15 states reviewed so far.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/tenant-screening-report-comparison/">What each screening report includes</a></h3><p>SmartMove, TurboTenant, RentRedi, Rentec Direct and RentPrep: price, who pays, and the coverage gaps each one discloses.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/turbotenant-no-criminal-records-available/">"No criminal records are available"</a></h3><p>What that TurboTenant message can mean and what to do about it.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/alternatives-to-zillow-rental-manager-screening/">Alternatives to Zillow Rental Manager screening</a></h3><p>Zillow charges the applicant $40 and nothing to the landlord. What Apartments.com, Avail, SmartMove and the rest include, and who pays.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/oregon-tenant-screening-rules/">Oregon tenant screening rules</a></h3><p>One screening charge per 60 days, the written notice you owe first, which evictions and convictions you can't consider, and the 14-day denial letter.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/phased-tenant-screening-jurisdictions/">Phased (two-step) screening</a></h3><p>Cook County, D.C., New York City and New Jersey: when the criminal check is allowed, the look-back periods and who is exempt.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/eviction-records-official-court-portals/">Eviction records: official court portals</a></h3><p>Free court searches in PA, WI, MN, MA, WA and MO, and the laws that hide eviction records in CA, MN, WA and elsewhere.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/tenant-screening-cost-calculator/">Screening cost calculator</a></h3><p>Landlord pays vs. applicant pays, per vacancy and per year, using each provider's published prices.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/rent-collection-app-fees/">Rent collection app fees</a></h3><p>ACH and card fees, who pays them, and payout days on TurboTenant, RentRedi, Rentec Direct and Avail.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/reusable-tenant-screening-reports-by-state/">Reusable screening reports by state</a></h3><p>Where landlords must accept an applicant's own report, and where a recent report waives the fee: CO, WA, CA, NY, RI, WI.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/smartmove-criminal-eviction-coverage-by-state/">SmartMove coverage by state</a></h3><p>All 50 states and D.C.: where SmartMove's criminal and eviction reports can return records, and the counties with limited eviction coverage.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/adverse-action-notice-tenant-screening/">Adverse action notices</a></h3><p>What federal law requires you to send after a screening report affects your decision, plus Washington's form and Oregon's 14-day rule.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/bank-linked-income-verification-what-landlords-see/">Bank-linked income verification</a></h3><p>What the landlord sees when an applicant connects a bank or payroll account on RentRedi, TurboTenant and SmartMove.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/prepaid-rent-limits-by-state/">Prepaid rent limits</a></h3><p>Can you take six months up front? The rules in California, Massachusetts, New York, Hawaii and Oregon.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/holding-deposits-and-admin-fees-by-state/">Holding deposits and admin fees</a></h3><p>Which states cap holding deposits or bar extra move-in fees: WA, OR, CA, MA, HI and NY.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/written-tenant-screening-criteria-by-state/">Written screening criteria</a></h3><p>Where you must hand applicants your screening rules before charging a fee: Oregon, Washington, Minnesota and California.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/screening-guarantors-and-co-signers/">Screening guarantors and co-signers</a></h3><p>Consent, fees and fee caps for guarantors, and how TurboTenant, RentRedi and SmartMove screen them.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/tenant-screening-without-ssn-itin/">Applicants without an SSN</a></h3><p>Which screening services accept an ITIN, and Oregon's and California's rules on ID and immigration status.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/rent-reporting-services-compared/">Rent reporting compared</a></h3><p>Which apps report rent to which bureaus, the price, who pays, and California's offer requirement.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/medical-debt-on-tenant-credit-reports/">Medical debt on credit reports</a></h3><p>What the three bureaus removed since 2022, and the New York, Minnesota and California laws that go further.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/previous-landlord-references-and-the-fcra/">Previous-landlord references</a></h3><p>When a reference call is just a call, when it becomes an FCRA report, and the CA, WA, OR and MN rules on reference checks.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/source-of-income-and-voucher-rules-by-state/">Section 8 and source-of-income rules</a></h3><p>Where you can't refuse a voucher, and how income minimums and credit checks apply to the tenant's share: WA, OR, CA, MA, MN.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/free-tenant-screening-report-copy/">Free copy of your screening report</a></h3><p>For applicants: when a tenant screening file is free, and how to request one from SmartMove, SafeRent, RealPage and others.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/screening-fee-refund-when-no-screening/">Screening fee refunds</a></h3><p>Charged a fee but never screened? Refund deadlines and penalties in CA, OR, MN, MD and WA.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/how-long-tenant-screening-takes/">How long screening takes</a></h3><p>Turnaround, common delays and how long you can view the report on SmartMove, TurboTenant, RentRedi and Rentec Direct.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/california-tenant-screening-rules/">California screening rules</a></h3><p>Credit and criminal checks are legal in California. The fee cap, the 7-day report copy, voucher-holder credit rules and the criminal-history limits.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/illinois-rental-fee-rules-2027/">Illinois rental fee rules for 2027</a></h3><p>The $50 application fee limit, the 14-day receipt rule, first-page fee disclosure and the banned junk fees.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/reporting-unpaid-rent-to-credit-bureaus/">Reporting unpaid rent to credit bureaus</a></h3><p>FCRA furnisher duties, the 7-year limit, California's notice rule, and how FrontLobby's debt reporting works.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/how-long-to-keep-tenant-screening-reports/">Keeping and destroying screening reports</a></h3><p>The FTC Disposal Rule, each platform's viewing window, and disposal laws in CA, MA and OR.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/rental-listing-scams-no-credit-check/">Rental listing scams</a></h3><p>"No credit check" ads, $1 credit-check links and copied listings, from the FTC's 2025 data, and what landlords can do.</p></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
  <p>Screening services are sold as "nationwide," but what comes back depends on where the rental is. TransUnion's <Aff id="smartmove" href="https://smartmove.pxf.io/c/6593174/1515180/17713" text="SmartMove" />, for example, publishes a list of the 30 states where its criminal records can currently be returned (<a href="https://www.mysmartmove.com/disclaimer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SmartMove disclaimer</a>). Landlords often find out about these gaps only after a blank report. We put the rules and the coverage in one place, by state.</p>
  <p><a href="/about/">How we research and what we won't do →</a></p>
</Base>
